# Tasks Rules

## Shortcode Syntax

Format: `[relation:type:identifier]` or `[type:identifier]` when relation is implied

Examples:
- `[task:001]` – reference to task
- `[adr:003]` – reference to decision
- `[lesson:context-overload]` – reference to lesson
- `[procedure:task-achieving]` – reference to procedure
- `used_in:[task:005, content:tooltips]` – used in multiple places
- `depends_on:[adr:001, task:003]` – dependencies

## Task Metadata (MDC Header)

```yaml
---
name: string              # Required – descriptive task name
number: integer           # Required – unique ID (can be auto-generated)
status: enum              # Required – [idea|backlog|task|wip|done|deferred]
type: enum                # [feature|bugfix|refactor|chore|docs|test|style|perf]
scope: enum               # [docs|design|deploy|build|content|code]
priority: enum            # [low|medium|high|critical]
effort: enum              # [xs|sm|md|lg|xl]
created: date             # YYYY-MM-DD (ISO)
modified: date            # YYYY-MM-DD (ISO)
dependencies: array       # [type:id, type:id]
related_tasks: array      # [task:NNN, task:MMM]
context_files: array      # [path/to/file.mdc]
tags: array               # [tag1, tag2, tag3]
resolution: string        # For done/deferred: [accepted|rejected|deferred|completed]
---
```

## Task Metadata

### Required Fields
- `name` – Descriptive task name
- `number` – Unique 3-digit integer (001, 002, ...)
- `status` – Current state [idea|backlog|ready-to-do|task|wip|done|deferred]

### Recommended Fields
- `type` – [feature|bugfix|refactor|chore|docs|test|style|perf]
- `created` – ISO date when task was created

### Optional Fields
- `scope`, `priority`, `effort`, `modified`, `dependencies`, `related_tasks`, `context_files`, `tags`, `resolution`

Add fields as needed for your workflow.

## Procedures and Artifacts

- Define tasks under `.cursor/tasks/` using the metadata above.
- Follow `[procedure:task-defining]` to create tasks (see `./.cursor/procedures/task-defining.mdc`).
- Follow `[procedure:task-achieving]` to complete tasks (see `./.cursor/procedures/task-achieving.mdc`).
- Upon completion, generate a `#runbook` in `.cursor/runbooks/` for the task.
- If a reusable insight emerges, extract a `#lesson` into `.cursor/lessons/` and cross-link.

### Execution Policy

- Do not start work outside a `task-NNN.mdc`.
- Refine the task until it is `ready-to-do` before execution.
- Use the specific procedures: `task-defining.mdc` for setup, `task-achieving.mdc` for execution.
- Maintain a runbook during/after execution and keep task status up to date.
  - Runbook jest obowiązkowy dla wszystkich zadań, w tym konfiguracji/porządków (zob. `./.cursor/procedures/task-achieving.mdc`).

### Interlinking Requirement

- Always interlink artifacts using shortcodes: tasks ↔ procedures ↔ runbooks ↔ lessons.
- Example: In task body, reference `[procedure:task-achieving]`; in runbook, reference `[task:NNN]` and any `[lesson:name]`.

## Indexing and Automation

- INDEX files (e.g., `INDEX.yaml`) should be generated by scripts, not hand-maintained.
- See `./.cursor/rules/mcp-future.mdc` for indexing script vision using TypeScript.

